type":"text","text":" function has been started (or is about to be started). This is used to prevent the destructor from running concurrently with the partial destructor. This can easily happen when the last strong pointer release its reference in one thread and starts the partialDestructor, while in another thread the last weak pointer goes out of scope and starts the destructor while the partialDestructor is still running. Both a start and finished bit is needed to handle a corner-case where the last strong pointer goes out of scope, then then last "},{"type":"code","text":"weakPointer"},{"type":"text","text":" goes out of scope, but this happens before the "},{"type":"code","text":"partialDestructor"},{"type":"text","text":" bit is set. It would be possible to use a single bit if it could also be set atomically when the strong count goes to zero and the weak count is non-zero, but that would add complexity (and likely slow down common cases as well)."}],[{"type":"text","text":"Partial destroy finished bit. This bit is set when the "},{"type":"code","text":"partialDestructor"},{"type":"text","text":" has finished running. See (3) above for more information."}]]}],"returns":null,"notes":[],"suppressionReason":null,"inheritedFrom":null},"location":{"declaration":{"file":"include/xrpl/basics/IntrusiveRefCounts.h","line":136},"definition":{"file":"include/xrpl/basics/IntrusiveRefCounts.h","line":136,"endLine":136}},"corrections":[],"type":[{"text":"std::atomic<"},{"text":"FieldType","target":{"path":"xrpl/IntrusiveRefCounts/FieldType","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"text":">"}],"initializer":[{"text":"{"},{"text":"kStrongDelta","target":{"path":"xrpl/IntrusiveRefCounts/kStrongDelta","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"text":"}"}],"bitfield":null,"qualifiers":{"isStatic":false,"isConstexpr":false,"isMutable":true},"declaration":[{"text":"mutable std::atomic<"},{"text":"FieldType","target":{"path":"xrpl/IntrusiveRefCounts/FieldType","resolution":"doxygen"}},{"text":"> refCounts_{"},{